From 568f06f37575fb4f1a0db4373b81b23a82946a02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:04:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: native output in sync with the sound as the
 ordinary output, and its A/V offset in the log

The render manager chooses a frame for the latency that Kodi takes, three
refresh periods (the buffers plus one), the same for every way of presenting
it. The ordinary output flips a frame two periods after the pass that chose
it (the pass waits for the flip of the frame before and commits without
waiting), and so does a frame of native Dolby Vision presented a frame ahead,
which CDVAhead had chosen one period earlier still. A frame presented the way
that waits commits and returns with its flip, one period after it was chosen.
So native output went out one period before its sound compared with the
ordinary output, with and without frames ahead: in the hardware test of 1.0
RC4 the flips of the two ways within 4 ms of each other, and 50 to 77 ms
before those of the ordinary output of the same title at 23.976 Hz on the AMD
integrated graphics (one period of 41.7 ms by the code, plus where in its
period each playback starts).

GetFrameLatencyAdjustment() now has a frame of native output presented the
way that waits chosen one period later than the latency says, and one
presented a frame ahead as the ordinary output (DVFrameLatencyAdjustmentMs()),
from the first frame of native output to its end. Which frames are shown at
which refresh rate does not change: only which refresh a frame starts at, by
one, as native output starts or ends or frames ahead come or go.

The jump of a period within a session of the RTX 4080 (the flips against the
player's clock from -72 to -114 ms after a step seek) is, read in the code,
not one of the picture against the sound: with the refresh rate equal to the
frame rate the render manager moves the clock by the phase of the frames
against the vblanks (SetVsyncAdjust()), the audio engine plays the sound by
that clock with its adjustment (CAudioSinkAE::GetClock()), and after a seek
the phase changes, the flips against the clock with it, and the picture
against its sound does not. What the log gave was the flips against the
clock. Now the render manager tells the window system also when the sound of
a frame is played, and every 10 s, with the line of native output, kodi.log
gives the A/V offset of each way, and the minute line of the ordinary output
too: "DVBridge: A/V in the last 10 s: the picture went out against its sound
by -41.9 ms (...) over 240 frames, the way that waits (positive: after it; at
the output of this computer, before the display)".

Host test (av_test.cpp: the choice of the render manager and the timing of
each way, 6 refresh rates, 37 phases, with and without the clock's
adjustment): the three ways at the same A/V offset for every phase, the old
adjustments one period early, the A/V offset steady where the flips against
the clock move by a period; 6 mutations caught.
